2. S3 bucket create karo

AWS Console → S3 → Create bucket

Example: 
my-company-ec2-backups

Bucket ko public mat karo.

Recommended:

    Block Public Access: ON

    Versioning: requirement ke according

    Encryption: SSE-S3 ya SSE-KMS

    Bucket region: EC2 ke same region mein rakhna convenient hota hai

3. EC2 ko IAM Role do

EC2 Ubuntu ko S3 access chahiye.

IAM mein role banao:

EC2BackupRole

Aur usko S3 par minimum required permissions do.

Example policy:

{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "s3:PutObject",
        "s3:ListBucket"
      ],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::my-company-ec2-backups",
        "arn:aws:s3:::my-company-ec2-backups/*"
      ]
    }
  ]
}

Phir EC2 instance ke saath ye IAM role attach kar do.

Important: EC2 ke andar AWS access key/secret key hard-code karne ki zarurat nahi hai.
IAM Instance Role use karna better hai.
4. Ubuntu par AWS CLI check karo

aws --version

Agar installed nahi hai:

sudo apt update
sudo apt install awscli -y

Check karo:

aws sts get-caller-identity

Agar IAM role correctly attached hai to AWS account/role information show hogi.
5. 500 GB data ka backup banao

Example maan lo actual data:

/var/www

Aap archive bana sakte ho:

sudo tar -czf /backup/website-backup.tar.gz /var/www

Lekin 500 GB ke liye blindly ek huge .tar.gz banana ideal nahi hai.

Better approach application/database ke according backup karna hai.

For example MySQL hai to pehle database dump:

mysqldump -u root -p mydatabase > /backup/mydatabase.sql

Aur application files separately backup karo.
6. S3 mein upload

Example:

aws s3 cp /backup/website-backup.tar.gz \
s3://my-company-ec2-backups/ec2-a/

Large file ke case mein AWS CLI multipart upload use kar sakta hai.

Upload verify:

aws s3 ls s3://my-company-ec2-backups/ec2-a/

7. Windows Server par AWS CLI install karo

Windows Server par AWS CLI install karke:

aws --version

Phir authenticate karna hoga.

Agar Windows Server AWS ke bahar/on-premises hai, to IAM credentials ko securely configure karna padega.

For example:

aws configure

Ye maangega:

AWS Access Key ID
AWS Secret Access Key
Default region
Output format

Access keys ko script mein directly hard-code mat karo.

Agar aapke environment mein AWS IAM Identity Center, federation, ya koi centralized credential mechanism available hai, woh preferable ho sakta hai.
8. S3 se Windows Server par download

Suppose Windows Server par destination:

D:\AWS-Backups

Command:

aws s3 cp s3://my-company-ec2-backups/ec2-a/ D:\AWS-Backups\ --recursive

500 GB data download hoga.

Check:

dir D:\AWS-Backups

9. Daily automatic backup

Ubuntu par script bana sakte ho:

sudo nano /usr/local/bin/ec2-backup.sh

Example:

#!/bin/bash

DATE=$(date +%Y-%m-%d)
BACKUP_DIR="/backup"
S3_BUCKET="s3://my-company-ec2-backups/ec2-a"

tar -czf "$BACKUP_DIR/backup-$DATE.tar.gz" /var/www

aws s3 cp "$BACKUP_DIR/backup-$DATE.tar.gz" \
"$S3_BUCKET/"

rm -f "$BACKUP_DIR/backup-$DATE.tar.gz"

Permission:

sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/ec2-backup.sh

Test:

sudo /usr/local/bin/ec2-backup.sh

10. Cron se daily run

Cron open karo:

sudo crontab -e

Daily 2 AM:

0 2 * * * /usr/local/bin/ec2-backup.sh >> /var/log/ec2-backup.log 2>&1

Ab backup automatically daily chalega.
11. Retention

Maan lo aapko 30 days ka backup rakhna hai.

S3 Lifecycle Rule bana sakte ho:

0–30 days      → S3 Standard
30–90 days     → S3 Standard-IA
90+ days       → Glacier / delete according to policy

500 GB ke environment mein lifecycle policies se storage cost control ki ja sakti hai.
12. Windows Server par daily download

Windows Task Scheduler se AWS CLI command schedule kar sakte ho:

aws s3 sync s3://my-company-ec2-backups/ec2-a/ D:\AWS-Backups\

sync useful hai kyunki har baar unnecessarily same files ko download nahi karta.
